ease mention I'll tag as \"G6PD deficiency.\" I'm still deciding how to handle \"haemolysis\" and will likely include it marked as excluded under the biological-process rule.\n\nI'm settling the annotation for the G6PD passage: \"enzyme deficiency\" as a general term to include but flag as excluded, \"haemolysis\" as a biological process also flagged excluded, and \"G6PD deficiency\" as the clear specific disease mention to keep. I'm working out the character offsets for each span against the source text.\n\nI'm reconsidering whether \"haemolysis\" should be treated as a disease class instead, but I'm leaning toward keeping it as a specific disease marked as excluded.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":213,\"end\":230,\"text\":\"enzyme deficiency\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"'enzyme deficiency' is a broad, non-specific term for a category of enzyme-related deficiencies rather than one named disease; general terms such as 'deficiency' are excluded.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate, 4. Do not annotate general terms\",\"excluded\":\"yes\"},{\"start\":260,\"end\":270,\"text\":\"haemolysis\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"'haemolysis' is mentioned as a sign and refers to a pathological process (red blood cell destruction) rather than a named disease; included as a borderline disease reading, but it is a biological process.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate, 5. Do not annotate references to biological processes\",\"excluded\":\"yes\"},{\"start\":430,\"end\":445,\"text\":\"G6PD deficiency\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"'G6PD deficiency' (glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency) is a named specific disease with one definition and no further categorization, referred to as a common type of deficiency in the sentence.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate, 1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions\",\"excluded\":\"no\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": nul